From 5ad4b99a061b0f84358f9111ef3cc72135ed5363 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artyom Shalkhakov <artyom.shalkhakov@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:34:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Forget an attribute's private document once it is freed

A prefixed attribute made before it is in a tree gets a private
document, recorded in its `detached` ivar so that -dealloc frees it.
-addAttribute: moves the attribute into the element's document and frees
the private one, but leaves `detached` pointing at it. -_insertChild:
clears it in the same situation; -addAttribute: did not.

Once another document is allocated at the freed address -- which glibc
soon does -- the stale pointer matches the document the attribute is in,
and -detach takes the attribute for already detached and returns without
unlinking it. When its element is torn down, the element's -dealloc
detaches its sub-nodes, the attribute stays in the tree, the tree is
freed, and the attribute object's own -dealloc then writes into the
freed node:

    malloc_consolidate(): unaligned fastbin chunk detected

Clear `detached` when the document it names is freed.

There is no test in the suite for this: whether the freed address is
reused depends on the allocator and on what else the process allocates,
and the test harness's pattern does not reuse it, so a test passes with
and without the change. repro-attribute-private-doc.m, which builds and
frees trees of elements with prefixed attributes, aborts within a few
thousand of them without the change and runs through with it; AddressSanitizer
and glibc's malloc checking both hide the fault by not reusing the
address.
---
 Source/NSXMLElement.m | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/NSXMLElement.m b/Source/NSXMLElement.m
index 74842090a..ef3d1cd3e 100644
--- a/Source/NSXMLElement.m
+++ b/Source/NSXMLElement.m
@@ -329,6 +329,10 @@ GS_PRIVATE_INTERNAL(NSXMLElement)
 #else
       xmlSetTreeDoc((xmlNodePtr)attr, theNode->doc);
 #endif
+      if (tmp == GSIVar(attribute, detached))
+        {
+          GSIVar(attribute, detached) = 0;
+        }
       xmlFreeDoc(tmp);
 
       oldAttr = xmlHasNsProp(theNode, attr->name, ns->href);
-- 
